  Why ColossalAI needed its own approach
                                        
  The paper (§4.2 Cluster Detector) explains the motivation:
                                                                                                                          
  ▎ "Alpa assumes the communication bandwidth between devices in the same computing node are the same. However, there are 
  ▎ some clusters that only have NVLink between 4 pairs of adjacent GPUs."                                                
                                                                                                                          
  ColossalAI's AlphaBetaProfiler was specifically designed to handle non-uniform intra-node topology (partial NVLink      
  coverage). That's why it actually measures pair-wise α/β instead of assuming all intra-node GPUs are equal. The tradeoff
   is that this measured data feeds search_best_logical_mesh() which requires a clean global rectangular grid —           
  introducing the power-of-2 constraint that Alpa avoids.

  ---
  Summary of my original claim
                                                                                                                          
  My earlier claim — "Alpa profiles each submesh independently" — is confirmed but should be more precise:
                                                                                                                          
  - Alpa profiles each (stage, submesh) pair by compiling and running the actual plan (real latency measurement)          
  - Alpa does not do global pair-wise α/β benchmarking                                                                    
  - ColossalAI does global pair-wise α/β benchmarking first, then uses those values analytically in the cost model (no    
  actual execution profiling during search)                                                                               
   
  These are two genuinely different profiling philosophies: Alpa is empirical per candidate, ColossalAI is analytical with
   upfront measurements.

